Current Dev Position: 1.9 Milestone 3 (M3)

Next Deadline: M3 cut off of August 24th at noon GMT (On hold until most li=
kely next week)


SWAT team rotation: Beth -> Saul

https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Yocto_Build_Failure_Swat_Team


Key Status/Updates:

*         M3/Feature freeze is still being worked on and continues to be de=
layed. Many things have merged but there are issues being encountered in so=
me areas.

*         Test builds are continuing as fast as the infrastructure allows u=
s to validate changes and get them merged.

*         The qemuarm segfault has been resolved.

*         Issues have been encountered in the sdk testing, particularly aar=
ch64 and those are being addressed. It has highlighted issues with the QA i=
nfrastructure as well.

*         There were significant issues found  with SIGKILL handling this w=
eek and those have also been resolved.

*         The mips lsb-sdk sanity test failures look like they're due to mi=
ps being incredibly slow at running some of the tests and it appears those =
tests have never been run up until some recent configuration changes.

*         There does appear to be a significant cpu usage issue when runnin=
g some of the automated QA tests which also doesn't help our overloaded inf=
rastructure.

*         Reminder: The current version that is in development will launch =
as YP 2.0 in October, 2015. We have renamed YP 1.9 M4 to YP 2.0.  This will=
 be the stabilization milestone for YP 2.0 release.

*         Since we have passed YP 1.9 M3; we are at YP 1.9 / 2.0 feature fr=
eeze.   All enhancements now will be pushed YP 2.1.

*         The release name for YP 2.0 is 'jethro'.


Key YP 1.9/2.0 Dates:

YP 1.9 M3 Release Target: Before Sept. 11 2015  (Will be late)

YP 2.0 Final - 2.0 Cut off: Sept. 28, 2015 noon GMT

YP 2.0 final Release Target: Before Oct. 30, 2015


Key Status Links for YP:

https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Yocto_Project_v1.9_Status

https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Yocto_1.9_Schedule

https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Yocto_1.9_Features


